  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Baobab Producers in Southern Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">One of the most iconic African trees the baobab, grows in inhospitable and arid areas. It offers a vital source of income for households who use a range of its products for consumption and sale. Phytotrade Africa, based in Zimbabwe, is a trade association with nearly 60 members across Southern Africa. They are involved in the collection, processing and marketing of natural products made from indigenous plants. Alongside two of its members, Tree Crops Malawi and Specialty Foods Africa, Phytotrade has invested in the development of collection, production and marketing of baobab products against a backdrop of growing regional and international demand for these products. Project activities will support all parts of the emerging supply chain. The collectors, 80% of whom are women, will learn more about quality control and how to organise together. The processors will achieve international hygiene and safety standards and become more efficient. Marketing activities will start to establish certified or &#x2018;ethical baobab&apos; with consumers and secure contracts for baobab powder, increasing volumes sold from 5 to 200 tonnes in the lifetime of the project. Trading to the targeted projections would make a significant addition to each producer&apos;s annual income.</narrative>
  </description>
